WEBVTT

00:01:44.437 --> 00:01:46.856
What is this?

00:02:00.328 --> 00:02:02.288
What's wrong with them?

00:02:02.288 --> 00:02:04.457
We've really stepped in it.

00:02:06.334 --> 00:02:08.128
Y-You guys...

00:02:09.629 --> 00:02:13.466
Hey, look. It's the high
schoolers who dropped out.

00:02:19.848 --> 00:02:22.517
What're you guys doing here?

00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.020
What are <i>you </i>doing up here?

00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.896
Shut up! It's got nothing
to do with you!

00:02:27.564 --> 00:02:28.815
I'll kill you!

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.191
What'd you say?

00:02:30.191 --> 00:02:32.986
If you're so tough,
show us what you've got!

00:02:32.986 --> 00:02:34.696
Fine with me!

00:02:56.593 --> 00:02:57.927
He reeks of alcohol.

00:02:59.012 --> 00:03:00.180
Who are you?

00:03:08.563 --> 00:03:10.440
You're late, kids.

00:03:13.318 --> 00:03:15.362
Welcome to hell...

00:03:16.488 --> 00:03:19.574
...you losers.

00:03:20.158 --> 00:03:26.164
"Start From Zero"

00:03:31.503 --> 00:03:32.796
I'm Mifune.

00:03:35.465 --> 00:03:39.052
I can't believe I have to
take care of you trash.

00:03:39.636 --> 00:03:42.889
What a pain in the ass.

00:03:47.811 --> 00:03:49.562
Our coach is a drunk?

00:03:49.938 --> 00:03:53.733
Listen up. My orders
are absolute up here.

00:03:54.317 --> 00:03:56.069
I'll throw anyone who disobeys me

00:03:56.069 --> 00:03:57.654
over the edge of that cliff.

00:03:59.322 --> 00:04:01.074
You heard him.

00:04:01.408 --> 00:04:06.204
I'm not too sure you
middle schoolers will make it

00:04:06.204 --> 00:04:08.790
through the training up here, though.

00:04:09.374 --> 00:04:13.586
I won't blame you if you run.

00:04:21.469 --> 00:04:22.303
Hey.

00:04:23.430 --> 00:04:27.392
You guys who lost to those
middle schoolers aren't

00:04:27.392 --> 00:04:28.935
in any position to talk.

00:04:28.935 --> 00:04:30.311
What?

00:04:30.311 --> 00:04:32.355
Hurry up and move, trash.

00:04:33.189 --> 00:04:35.150
Training starts now.

00:04:58.298 --> 00:05:00.258
You trash finished changing?

00:05:00.675 --> 00:05:02.052
What's your problem?

00:05:02.052 --> 00:05:04.387
Why do you keep calling us trash?

00:05:04.387 --> 00:05:05.347
We're not--

00:05:05.347 --> 00:05:06.681
Trash is trash.

00:05:06.681 --> 00:05:07.724
What?

00:05:07.724 --> 00:05:08.850
Or

00:05:09.684 --> 00:05:13.646
would you prefer I call you losers?

00:05:17.650 --> 00:05:20.737
Start by digging some holes.
Make 'em deep.

00:05:21.154 --> 00:05:21.988
Holes?

00:05:23.615 --> 00:05:25.617
I'll be back in an hour.

00:05:28.787 --> 00:05:30.497
Hey, high schoolers.

00:05:31.081 --> 00:05:32.999
You guys will be climbing
up the waterfall.

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:34.542
Hurry up and get ready.

00:05:34.542 --> 00:05:35.418
Yes, sir.

00:05:35.794 --> 00:05:39.339
That sounds fun. Take me with you.

00:05:40.799 --> 00:05:42.759
Hey, come on.

00:05:49.391 --> 00:05:50.850
Jerk.

00:05:51.393 --> 00:05:54.020
Well? What are we supposed to do?

00:05:54.646 --> 00:05:56.773
We just have to do it.

00:05:57.148 --> 00:06:00.443
If we don't, he'll push
us off the cliff.

00:06:06.658 --> 00:06:09.244
All right, stop.

00:06:11.871 --> 00:06:13.957
Why are you standing around?

00:06:14.374 --> 00:06:16.710
Go put your shovels away.

00:06:20.130 --> 00:06:22.007
That drunk bastard...

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:24.467
I wondered how he
was going to train us,

00:06:24.467 --> 00:06:25.927
but he just makes us dig holes?

00:06:26.428 --> 00:06:29.931
There's plenty of better
things we could be doing.

00:06:30.348 --> 00:06:32.100
Why is he making us dig holes?

00:06:33.351 --> 00:06:35.311
Let's head back.

00:06:43.653 --> 00:06:46.573
Okay, fill them up.

00:06:46.906 --> 00:06:49.492
You mean those holes...

00:06:49.909 --> 00:06:52.495
They were just for him to take a piss?

00:06:52.871 --> 00:06:55.999
Quit bitching and fill
the holes back in!

00:06:55.999 --> 00:06:58.418
Move it! Where are your shovels?!

00:07:00.628 --> 00:07:02.756
We just put them away.

00:07:03.256 --> 00:07:04.257
Damn it.

00:07:18.730 --> 00:07:21.274
Did you fill them completely, trash?

00:07:24.652 --> 00:07:27.489
Hey, our warm-up suits are missing.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:31.743
I thought we left them over there.

00:07:32.285 --> 00:07:33.453
They're right there.

00:07:34.871 --> 00:07:36.956
Under your feet.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.541
Our feet?

00:07:38.917 --> 00:07:40.001
You don't mean...

00:07:41.127 --> 00:07:43.254
Seriously?

00:07:44.798 --> 00:07:46.466
That's great.

00:07:47.050 --> 00:07:53.348
Your precious little warm-up suits
aren't worth anything up here.

00:07:53.348 --> 00:07:54.808
What'd you say?

00:07:55.225 --> 00:07:56.267
You bastard!

00:07:56.267 --> 00:07:57.811
I've had enough of you!

00:07:57.811 --> 00:07:59.229
No, Kaidoh!

00:07:59.604 --> 00:08:01.523
But, Kawamura-<i>senpai</i>, they...

00:08:01.523 --> 00:08:02.399
Kaidoh!

00:08:03.358 --> 00:08:05.694
Don't forget our goal.

00:08:23.211 --> 00:08:24.671
Pick up the pace!

00:08:24.963 --> 00:08:26.589
Move it!

00:08:37.684 --> 00:08:39.769
You're late, trash.

00:08:41.354 --> 00:08:43.189
All right, high schoolers.

00:08:43.523 --> 00:08:45.525
Take a minute to get some water.

00:09:12.218 --> 00:09:12.969
Wa...

00:09:14.804 --> 00:09:15.889
Water...

00:09:19.225 --> 00:09:21.102
Whoops, sorry.

00:09:22.020 --> 00:09:23.021
What was that for?

00:09:24.522 --> 00:09:27.317
That was refreshing.

00:09:28.360 --> 00:09:30.236
Good work.

00:09:31.821 --> 00:09:34.240
Wh-Where's our water?

00:09:34.657 --> 00:09:37.660
Looks like we'll have to
climb back down again.

00:09:54.886 --> 00:09:55.845
Listen up.

00:09:56.429 --> 00:09:59.265
If you drop your ball,
you're not getting dinner tonight.

00:09:59.766 --> 00:10:00.684
Begin!

00:10:01.017 --> 00:10:03.103
Why are we doing this?

00:10:03.728 --> 00:10:07.524
Burden on abdominal and
back muscles: 240%.

00:10:08.358 --> 00:10:11.528
It's gotta be some kind of
strengthening exercise.

00:10:36.177 --> 00:10:38.096
Here I come!

00:10:41.349 --> 00:10:42.600
You still have a long way to go.

00:10:42.851 --> 00:10:45.645
Koshimae, wait up!

00:10:52.027 --> 00:10:53.945
I'm so hungry.

00:10:53.945 --> 00:10:56.906
We haven't had breakfast yet.

00:10:57.657 --> 00:11:00.952
This is getting stupid.

00:11:02.037 --> 00:11:07.292
Is that drunk really one of the coaches?

00:11:08.835 --> 00:11:13.465
I wonder what they're doing right now.

00:11:14.007 --> 00:11:15.175
Who?

00:11:16.217 --> 00:11:18.178
The winners, of course.

00:11:23.224 --> 00:11:24.601
Damn it.

00:11:24.601 --> 00:11:27.062
While we're dealing with this nonsense,

00:11:27.062 --> 00:11:31.900
without having had breakfast, they're...

00:12:05.475 --> 00:12:07.143
I can't take this any more!

00:12:07.143 --> 00:12:09.062
How long are you guys
gonna take a break?

00:12:09.062 --> 00:12:12.023
Hey, someone get some water.

00:12:16.945 --> 00:12:19.406
Make it quick, kids.

00:12:22.742 --> 00:12:24.953
I'll go.

00:12:30.041 --> 00:12:31.918
I'll go too, Koshimae.

00:12:33.128 --> 00:12:35.380
You guys are full of energy, aren't you?

00:12:36.840 --> 00:12:39.300
I don't wanna lose to them.

00:12:43.013 --> 00:12:44.723
You're right, Echizen.

00:12:44.723 --> 00:12:48.852
I can't forgive those
high school bastards.

00:12:48.852 --> 00:12:50.228
I just can't.

00:12:50.937 --> 00:12:54.149
Yeah, the next time they give us crap,

00:12:54.149 --> 00:12:55.650
I'll make them regret it.

00:12:56.109 --> 00:12:58.528
We'll show them who's boss.

00:13:12.542 --> 00:13:14.836
How's that lot doing?

00:13:15.253 --> 00:13:18.131
That lot? You mean the losers?

00:13:19.257 --> 00:13:23.928
They should be training hard
in the mountains right now.

00:13:26.890 --> 00:13:30.852
But grit, grit, and more grit is such

00:13:30.852 --> 00:13:33.772
an antiquated philosophy.

00:13:36.316 --> 00:13:39.027
Humans are mysterious creatures.

00:13:39.402 --> 00:13:41.654
Hidden inside us is
something immeasurable

00:13:41.654 --> 00:13:44.449
even with the most
cutting edge technology.

00:13:45.325 --> 00:13:49.871
I wonder how much of
it is psychological.

00:13:50.163 --> 00:13:51.956
Figuring that out...

00:13:51.956 --> 00:13:54.918
...is my job as the mental coach.

00:13:59.297 --> 00:14:01.383
It'll be dark soon.

00:14:01.383 --> 00:14:05.261
We'll wrap up today's training
session and decide.

00:14:05.261 --> 00:14:07.138
Decide what?

00:14:07.764 --> 00:14:09.599
Where you'll be sleeping tonight.

00:14:10.475 --> 00:14:13.019
The cabin's only big enough for
either the high schoolers

00:14:13.019 --> 00:14:14.896
or the middle schoolers, not both.

00:14:14.896 --> 00:14:17.982
Are you saying...

00:14:18.233 --> 00:14:21.027
We'll play against the high schoolers,

00:14:21.027 --> 00:14:23.488
and the winners will sleep
in the cabin tonight, right?

00:14:24.155 --> 00:14:27.033
Of course. We'll play against
the high schoolers.

00:14:27.033 --> 00:14:28.034
Just so you know...

00:14:28.743 --> 00:14:32.247
The losers will sleep in the cave.

00:14:36.835 --> 00:14:43.091
It's the "High Schoolers vs. Middle
Schoolers Battle for Beds!"

00:14:43.091 --> 00:14:45.010
That's not much of a title.

00:14:45.593 --> 00:14:47.512
The rules are simple.

00:14:47.512 --> 00:14:50.181
Those who miss, step outside the court.

00:14:50.807 --> 00:14:53.351
The last one inside is the winner.

00:14:53.685 --> 00:14:57.063
Hold on. This isn't fair.

00:14:57.480 --> 00:14:58.940
Are you ready?

00:14:58.940 --> 00:15:02.277
We've got way less people than them.

00:15:02.610 --> 00:15:03.820
Let's get started.

00:15:04.404 --> 00:15:06.448
He's not listening.

00:15:06.865 --> 00:15:10.285
I don't think complaining
will do any good.

00:15:10.827 --> 00:15:12.245
Here, Taka-<i>san</i>.

00:15:14.497 --> 00:15:16.332
Burning!

00:15:16.332 --> 00:15:20.587
Even if we've got less
people, it's no problem!

00:15:20.587 --> 00:15:23.048
Hit me with your best shot!

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:25.383
That's the spirit.

00:15:25.842 --> 00:15:26.968
Begin.

00:15:29.846 --> 00:15:30.972
It's coming!

00:15:31.556 --> 00:15:32.515
I got it.

00:15:35.602 --> 00:15:37.145
An irregular bounce.

00:15:37.562 --> 00:15:39.022
You, out.

00:15:44.652 --> 00:15:46.321
You're out.

00:15:46.905 --> 00:15:47.530
Out.

00:15:47.822 --> 00:15:48.490
Out.

00:15:48.740 --> 00:15:49.366
Out!

00:15:49.657 --> 00:15:50.283
Out!

00:15:51.284 --> 00:15:54.162
This is a tough court to play on.

00:15:54.162 --> 00:15:57.207
You can't tell where
the ball will bounce.

00:15:57.457 --> 00:15:58.416
Here I come.

00:16:04.089 --> 00:16:06.883
Great! Momo, good hit!

00:16:10.595 --> 00:16:11.763
Out.

00:16:11.763 --> 00:16:14.724
You're too big, Tanishi-<i>san</i>.

00:16:15.100 --> 00:16:16.351
How pathetic.

00:16:16.351 --> 00:16:17.686
This is too easy.

00:16:19.854 --> 00:16:21.523
This isn't good.

00:16:21.523 --> 00:16:25.443
They know all the
irregularities of the court.

00:16:25.443 --> 00:16:28.071
We're at a disadvantage.

00:16:28.488 --> 00:16:29.948
Gather 'round, guys.

00:16:30.490 --> 00:16:31.991
I've got an idea.

00:16:42.502 --> 00:16:45.588
Hey, are you sure about that?

00:16:45.588 --> 00:16:47.382
They probably think they'll have an

00:16:47.382 --> 00:16:49.426
easier time hitting the
ball with fewer people.

00:16:49.718 --> 00:16:52.262
It won't be that easy!

00:16:54.389 --> 00:16:58.393
Don't underestimate
Naniwa's Speed Star.

00:16:59.853 --> 00:17:01.688
Great, Kenya-<i>san</i>.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.525
You're mine!

00:17:09.738 --> 00:17:10.864
Out.

00:17:11.114 --> 00:17:13.575
Damn it, they're just playing dirty.

00:17:13.575 --> 00:17:17.412
They've got more guys,
and it's always their serve.

00:17:17.412 --> 00:17:22.208
Yeah, but Matsudaira's serves
and Sasabe's smashes are...

00:17:23.168 --> 00:17:24.294
Yeah.

00:17:24.586 --> 00:17:27.964
Their power and control are
way better than before.

00:17:29.049 --> 00:17:32.802
On top of that, we're playing
on an irregular court.

00:17:35.638 --> 00:17:37.015
Bastards.

00:17:39.893 --> 00:17:41.895
We just have to make sure the
ball doesn't touch the ground.

00:17:42.395 --> 00:17:44.189
Yeah, just volley.

00:17:44.189 --> 00:17:46.608
I'd like to see you try!

00:17:54.157 --> 00:17:56.993
You two, out!

00:17:58.787 --> 00:18:01.081
Get outta my way, Koshimae.

00:18:01.998 --> 00:18:04.668
This is why I hate doubles.

00:18:04.668 --> 00:18:05.752
Oh, boy.

00:18:05.752 --> 00:18:09.339
The rookies of the West and the
East all have terrible teamwork.

00:18:09.714 --> 00:18:12.676
Okay, here I come!

00:18:14.678 --> 00:18:16.554
Fool!

00:18:20.392 --> 00:18:24.020
The kids are right!
We'll attack with a volley!

00:18:30.819 --> 00:18:34.781
H-He returned all of them.

00:18:34.781 --> 00:18:35.699
Bastard.

00:18:44.499 --> 00:18:46.793
Good work, old man.

00:18:47.085 --> 00:18:50.005
This'll be an easy win.
You guys are nothing special.

00:18:50.005 --> 00:18:52.132
Where'd all that confidence go?

00:18:57.929 --> 00:18:59.723
Have you input the terrain

00:18:59.723 --> 00:19:02.809
and angles of reflection, Sadaharu?

00:19:03.268 --> 00:19:07.230
Yes, Renji. I've got
all the data I need.

00:19:08.023 --> 00:19:10.817
Guys, could you step
off the court please?

00:19:12.152 --> 00:19:13.111
Inui,

00:19:13.820 --> 00:19:15.071
Yanagi.

00:19:15.905 --> 00:19:20.035
You've got a lot of guts to
send just two guys against us.

00:19:25.874 --> 00:19:26.708
What?

00:19:27.250 --> 00:19:31.588
My data is perfect.

00:19:37.594 --> 00:19:42.474
Chance of us missing due to
an irregular bounce: 0%.

00:19:42.474 --> 00:19:43.933
That's impossible.

00:19:43.933 --> 00:19:46.102
Is he saying they can

00:19:46.102 --> 00:19:48.021
predict which way the ball will bounce?

00:19:49.856 --> 00:19:52.150
Angle of incidence, 47 degrees.

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:54.027
Angle of reflection, 61 degrees.

00:19:54.027 --> 00:19:56.363
The spatial vector and
moment of inertia are...

00:19:58.448 --> 00:20:01.576
Air pressure, ground
composition, humidity...

00:20:01.868 --> 00:20:03.703
The impact timing is...

00:20:05.288 --> 00:20:08.750
Amazing, Yanagi-<i>san</i>, Inui-<i>senpai</i>.

00:20:08.750 --> 00:20:09.918
With that teamwork,

00:20:09.918 --> 00:20:11.544
it's hard to believe they're
from different schools.

00:20:12.879 --> 00:20:13.963
Not bad.

00:20:14.798 --> 00:20:17.384
U-Unbelievable.

00:20:18.218 --> 00:20:20.345
Shall we finish this?

00:20:20.345 --> 00:20:21.262
I suppose.

00:20:23.640 --> 00:20:25.225
That's enough.

00:20:25.475 --> 00:20:29.396
Two middle schoolers to
three high schoolers.

00:20:29.771 --> 00:20:32.148
The high schoolers win.

00:20:32.524 --> 00:20:33.817
All right!

00:20:33.817 --> 00:20:34.984
We did it!

00:20:36.236 --> 00:20:37.445
What are you talking about?

00:20:37.696 --> 00:20:41.157
There were more high
schoolers to begin with!

00:20:41.157 --> 00:20:46.079
Enough! If I say the high
schoolers won, they won!

00:20:46.538 --> 00:20:47.997
You got a problem with that?!

00:20:49.332 --> 00:20:50.250
No.

00:20:50.250 --> 00:20:51.251
We don't.

00:20:51.584 --> 00:20:53.169
Of course not!

00:20:53.545 --> 00:20:55.880
You kids are way too young to be

00:20:55.880 --> 00:20:57.590
talking back to Coach Nyudo!

00:20:58.508 --> 00:21:01.177
The high schoolers will prepare dinner,

00:21:01.177 --> 00:21:03.596
and the middle schoolers will clean up.

00:21:13.523 --> 00:21:14.441
Hey.

00:21:17.318 --> 00:21:19.154
You're Coach Nyudo?

00:21:20.030 --> 00:21:21.614
What about it?

00:21:24.784 --> 00:21:27.287
You should see Coach Nyudo.

00:21:31.374 --> 00:21:34.127
Don't talk to me if you've
got nothing to say.

00:23:17.063 --> 00:23:17.856
"Preview"

00:23:17.856 --> 00:23:19.607
"Preview"
Hey, you kids.

00:23:19.607 --> 00:23:20.567
"Preview"
I've got an important job for you to do.

00:23:20.567 --> 00:23:22.986
I've got an important job for you to do.

00:23:22.986 --> 00:23:24.362
What are you gonna make us do?

00:23:24.362 --> 00:23:27.449
I want you to sneak into
the training camp.

00:23:27.449 --> 00:23:30.118
Huh? You want us to do what?

00:23:30.118 --> 00:23:33.455
Don't you think it's
reckless to send us into

00:23:33.455 --> 00:23:34.789
that high security place?

00:23:34.789 --> 00:23:37.083
I don't wanna go.

00:23:39.544 --> 00:23:40.628
"Special Mission"
The next episode of <i>Prince</i>
<i>of Tennis II </i>is: "Special Mission."

00:23:40.628 --> 00:23:43.631
"Special Mission"
Quit your whining and move!

00:23:43.631 --> 00:23:47.136
"Special Mission"
